# Git commit identity

When creating git commits for this project:

- **Author name:** `Mohammad Roustaei` (or the repo-local `user.name` if it already matches this person)
- **Author email:** `mrmaper78@gmail.com`
- **Committer** must be the same identity — never Cursor, Copilot, or any other tool/bot identity

## How to commit

Prefer the repo-local git config if it is already set to Mohammad Roustaei / mrmaper78@gmail.com.

Otherwise pass author/committer explicitly **without** changing git config permanently:

```bash
git -c user.name="Mohammad Roustaei" -c user.email="mrmaper78@gmail.com" commit ...
```

Or:

```bash
$env:GIT_AUTHOR_NAME="Mohammad Roustaei"
$env:GIT_AUTHOR_EMAIL="mrmaper78@gmail.com"
$env:GIT_COMMITTER_NAME="Mohammad Roustaei"
$env:GIT_COMMITTER_EMAIL="mrmaper78@gmail.com"
git commit ...
```

## Never

- Do not use Cursor / agent / noreply emails as author or committer
- Do not `git config` to overwrite the user's global identity unless they explicitly ask
- Do not amend someone else's commit to rewrite authorship unless they explicitly ask
